          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A right rectangular prism has a height of 9 inches. The length of the prism’$s$ base is $x$ inches,\nwhich is 7 inches more than the width of the prism’$s$ base. Which function $V$ gives the volume of\nthe prism, in cubic inches, in terms of the length of the prism’$s$ base?"
